1
00:00:01,181 --> 00:00:09,221
The Princess Sapphire
Knight of the Ribbon

2
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,160
♪ Atashi no miru yume himitsu nano ♪
The dreams I see are my secret

3
00:00:51,250 --> 00:00:57,089
♪ Dare ni mo iwanai himitsu nano ♪
I won’t tell anyone—it’s my secret

4
00:00:58,541 --> 00:01:02,461
♪ Akai manto hira hira ♪
A red cape fluttering

5
00:01:02,462 --> 00:01:04,981
♪ Uma o tobasu oujo ♪
Galloping on a horse—the princess

6
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:06,901
♪ Sore ga atashi ♪
That’s me!

7
00:01:07,621 --> 00:01:10,901
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

8
00:01:10,905 --> 00:01:13,424
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

9
00:01:14,541 --> 00:01:18,021
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

10
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:20,741
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

11
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:25,220
♪ Ribon no kishi wa ♪
The Knight of the Ribbon,

12
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:28,621
♪ Honto wa hontto wa ♪
Truly, truly,

13
00:01:28,622 --> 00:01:31,822
♪ Atashi nano sa ♪
It’s really me!

14
00:01:44,101 --> 00:01:50,141
Twenty-Fifth Episode
The King's Ghost
Banzai for the King!!

15
00:01:53,339 --> 00:01:58,980
<i>Before we start today's story, let's recap what happened last week.</i>

16
00:02:00,459 --> 00:02:03,865
<i>With the King missing and presumed dead,</i>

17
00:02:03,889 --> 00:02:07,251
<i>Sapphire succeeded him to the throne.</i>

18
00:02:07,275 --> 00:02:09,778
<i>However, the villainous Duralumin and Nylon schemed to reveal that</i>

19
00:02:09,802 --> 00:02:12,580
<i>Sapphire is actually a girl...</i>

20
00:02:12,581 --> 00:02:15,025
<i>...was exposed, and she was locked away</i>

21
00:02:15,049 --> 00:02:17,800
<i>in terrifying Coffin Tower along with the Queen.</i>

22
00:02:18,330 --> 00:02:20,880
<i>But the spirited Sapphire didn't back down.</i>

23
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:23,797
<i>She escaped through the hole the mice showed her</i>

24
00:02:23,847 --> 00:02:27,886
<i>and became the mysterious Ribbon Knight, to punish Duralumin!</i>

25
00:02:28,686 --> 00:02:31,391
<i>However, Duralumin suspected the Ribbon Knight was</i>

26
00:02:31,415 --> 00:02:33,497
<i>Sapphire and sent an assassin to the Coffin Tower,</i>

27
00:02:33,521 --> 00:02:37,580
<i>but they were easily driven off.</i>

28
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:47,560
<i>But the relentless Duralumin won't give up.</i>

29
00:02:48,886 --> 00:02:52,494
<i>This time, they bribe Gama,</i>

30
00:02:52,518 --> 00:02:56,366
<i>the wicked jailer of the Coffin Tower, to catch Sapphire off guard.</i>

31
00:02:58,575 --> 00:03:01,666
<i>Outside, a fierce storm rages with thunder and lightning.</i>

32
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:07,060
<i>Today's story begins just as Gama is about to attack Sapphire.</i>

33
00:03:18,163 --> 00:03:19,756
Gama!

34
00:04:29,401 --> 00:04:30,376
Thank you.

35
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:32,400
You saved Sapphire's life, didn't you?

36
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:34,260
What's wrong, Sapphire?

37
00:04:34,755 --> 00:04:36,900
Mother, Gama is knocked out cold.

38
00:04:37,265 --> 00:04:39,546
Oh dear, we must tend to him right away.

39
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:50,560
But what on earth did Gama do to you?

40
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:56,920
Oh, nothing really.

41
00:04:57,528 --> 00:04:58,005
No?

42
00:04:58,456 --> 00:05:00,240
He wasn't trying to take your life?

43
00:05:02,170 --> 00:05:03,880
Look, he's holding a dagger.

44
00:05:04,725 --> 00:05:07,093
Yeah, he probably got scared by a mouse and

45
00:05:07,117 --> 00:05:09,453
slipped trying to chase it off with his dagger.

46
00:05:09,840 --> 00:05:12,600
Quick, if we don't treat him, he'll die.

47
00:05:27,005 --> 00:05:29,040
He'll be fine now. I'm sure he'll recover.

48
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:30,780
I'll go boil some more water.

49
00:05:31,230 --> 00:05:32,860
Mother, I'll help you.

50
00:05:48,620 --> 00:05:49,826
You fool!

51
00:05:50,564 --> 00:05:52,150
Do it again!

52
00:05:52,175 --> 00:05:55,280
Their guard is down this time, so make sure you finish them off.

53
00:05:55,565 --> 00:05:56,640
Failure will not be tolerated.

54
00:05:58,570 --> 00:06:02,040
Come on, I'll strike from behind, too.

55
00:06:06,110 --> 00:06:07,873
There we go, Mother.

56
00:06:08,085 --> 00:06:09,085
Thank you.

57
00:06:29,910 --> 00:06:31,380
C-Curse you, intruder!

58
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:43,186
Gama, you saved us, didn't you?

59
00:06:46,050 --> 00:06:48,413
Gama, thank you, thank you so much!

60
00:06:48,925 --> 00:06:50,300
Thank you so very much.

61
00:06:50,417 --> 00:06:51,396
Ouch!

62
00:06:51,420 --> 00:06:53,719
Ouch! It hurts!

63
00:07:21,233 --> 00:07:21,493
Here.

64
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:27,013
Here, look.

65
00:07:31,030 --> 00:07:33,240
Hey Gama, mice are really cute, aren't they?

66
00:07:33,595 --> 00:07:36,080
Yeah, they really are cute.

67
00:07:43,650 --> 00:07:44,890
Thanks for the meal.

68
00:07:50,980 --> 00:07:52,680
Well, I'm off!

69
00:07:55,435 --> 00:07:57,160
Why, if it isn't the Ribbon Knight.

70
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:03,600
I'm not picking on Princess Sapphire anymore, I swear!

71
00:08:03,740 --> 00:08:08,020
It's true! I really have become a loyal servant to Princess Sapphire and the Queen.

72
00:08:13,420 --> 00:08:14,800
Oh, so that's how it was.

73
00:08:14,860 --> 00:08:16,140
Yeah, that's how it was.

74
00:08:16,370 --> 00:08:18,940
The enemies of the Ribbon Knight are that centipede Duralumin and Nylon.

75
00:08:19,225 --> 00:08:21,753
To take those two down, I'd even break into the castle.

76
00:08:24,020 --> 00:08:26,580
What a terrifying princess.

77
00:08:30,050 --> 00:08:32,860
Speaking of the castle, have you heard that rumor?

78
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:34,380
A rumor?

79
00:08:34,540 --> 00:08:40,366
They say that in the dead of night, the ghost of the late king appears.

80
00:08:41,209 --> 00:08:42,299
My father's ghost?

81
00:08:43,720 --> 00:08:46,050
Anyone who says they saw the ghost

82
00:08:46,075 --> 00:08:50,310
or spreads rumors about it is sent to the quarry as a slave.

83
00:08:50,334 --> 00:08:54,260
Then if I go to the quarry, I can find out more about Father's ghost.

84
00:09:18,510 --> 00:09:20,140
That's the entrance to the quarry.

85
00:09:20,505 --> 00:09:22,080
Security is pretty tight.

86
00:09:27,649 --> 00:09:29,153
Open up!

87
00:09:32,301 --> 00:09:33,865
Now's my chance.

88
00:09:33,889 --> 00:09:35,453
Close it!

89
00:09:37,940 --> 00:09:38,940
Hey you!

90
00:09:39,020 --> 00:09:39,673
Close it!

91
00:09:39,720 --> 00:09:40,720
Hurry and close it!

92
00:09:45,359 --> 00:09:47,486
Pardon me, but I'm coming through!

93
00:09:52,340 --> 00:09:53,400
Damn it!

94
00:10:22,980 --> 00:10:23,626
Take that!

95
00:10:23,719 --> 00:10:24,513
Cut them down!

96
00:10:24,640 --> 00:10:26,400
Take your work more seriously!

97
00:10:49,709 --> 00:10:51,480
My throat's parched!

98
00:10:51,969 --> 00:10:55,237
I wish the Ribbon Knight would show up here, too.

99
00:10:55,261 --> 00:10:56,320
Ribbon Knight...

100
00:10:56,565 --> 00:10:58,566
Don't be ridiculous, Ribbon Knight.

101
00:10:58,639 --> 00:11:02,000
That's just a children's fantasy, a dream. There's no way he exists.

102
00:11:02,285 --> 00:11:04,260
Reality is much harsher.

103
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:08,273
We'll just end up drying up in the sun out here.

104
00:11:12,788 --> 00:11:17,348
Water?! No, it's impossible!
Reality is something else!

105
00:11:17,699 --> 00:11:20,333
This is probably just an illusion too.

106
00:11:21,355 --> 00:11:22,128
Why?

107
00:11:24,180 --> 00:11:26,280
Who splashed water on me?

108
00:11:27,419 --> 00:11:28,460
Water! It's water!

109
00:11:31,560 --> 00:11:32,920
It's real water!

110
00:11:37,080 --> 00:11:39,939
Hey, how dare you steal our water!

111
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:42,920
Stop!

112
00:11:48,139 --> 00:11:49,393
Stop picking on the weak!

113
00:11:50,130 --> 00:11:52,093
That kid... Could it be the Ribbon Knight?

114
00:11:52,765 --> 00:11:54,860
Where are you hiding?

115
00:11:54,885 --> 00:11:56,360
Come out!

116
00:12:01,179 --> 00:12:02,179
Ribbon Knight!

117
00:12:04,013 --> 00:12:06,540
Don't let him get away!

118
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:28,406
Come on, let's get him!

119
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:51,380
Alright!

120
00:12:51,595 --> 00:12:53,700
In return, unchain everyone!

121
00:12:57,380 --> 00:12:58,020
Uranari!

122
00:12:58,280 --> 00:12:58,740
Garigori!

123
00:12:58,845 --> 00:12:59,845
Nanny!

124
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:01,840
How do you know our names...?

125
00:13:09,799 --> 00:13:11,046
P-Princess Sapphire!

126
00:13:12,389 --> 00:13:13,999
Prince Sapphire!

127
00:13:14,271 --> 00:13:16,880
I'm so happy that you are safe!

128
00:13:17,020 --> 00:13:17,820
Come on, hurry up!

129
00:13:17,930 --> 00:13:19,860
Wait, before that, there's something I want to ask.

130
00:13:20,025 --> 00:13:21,380
About my father's ghost.

131
00:13:21,969 --> 00:13:23,440
I've heard about that.

132
00:13:23,780 --> 00:13:29,346
Anyone who heard the King's voice or spread rumors was sent here.

133
00:13:30,779 --> 00:13:32,040
They heard his voice and footsteps?

134
00:13:32,430 --> 00:13:33,620
So nobody actually saw him?

135
00:13:33,960 --> 00:13:34,406
That's right.

136
00:13:34,775 --> 00:13:36,753
No one has actually seen him.

137
00:13:37,060 --> 00:13:42,193
Every night around midnight, the King's voice and footsteps come from the basement...

138
00:13:42,427 --> 00:13:43,554
<i>...from the basement...</i>

139
00:13:51,629 --> 00:13:55,013
It's about time the King's ghost starts walking around down there...

140
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:02,159
It's almost time...

141
00:14:16,279 --> 00:14:19,760
Under the lion ornament, the third stone...

142
00:14:20,116 --> 00:14:21,233
One, two, three...

143
00:14:22,711 --> 00:14:23,701
This is it!

144
00:14:50,494 --> 00:14:51,893
Here we go...

145
00:14:53,599 --> 00:14:54,593
It's the tomb...

146
00:15:04,359 --> 00:15:05,486
It's midnight...

147
00:15:22,439 --> 00:15:23,433
Father's voice...

148
00:15:57,611 --> 00:15:58,893
Father...

149
00:16:01,984 --> 00:16:02,853
Father...

150
00:16:05,899 --> 00:16:06,899
Father!

151
00:16:07,689 --> 00:16:08,689
Who's there?

152
00:16:09,700 --> 00:16:10,460
You're alive?

153
00:16:10,586 --> 00:16:11,326
Father...

154
00:16:13,929 --> 00:16:15,160
Is that you, Sapphire...?

155
00:16:15,929 --> 00:16:17,008
Father...

156
00:16:17,032 --> 00:16:19,746
So you survived as well...

157
00:16:20,909 --> 00:16:23,179
Father, Mother is safe and well, too...

158
00:16:23,429 --> 00:16:25,128
I see. I missed you...

159
00:16:25,152 --> 00:16:27,320
But who could it be?

160
00:16:31,811 --> 00:16:33,580
Who trapped you in a place like this?

161
00:16:33,885 --> 00:16:34,398
I don't know.

162
00:16:35,120 --> 00:16:37,500
I couldn't see what they looked like at all.

163
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:40,855
That night—the night I was attacked—

164
00:16:40,880 --> 00:16:44,806
I was in my room writing an important decree.

165
00:17:03,640 --> 00:17:07,488
Thrown into this dungeon by an unknown enemy,

166
00:17:07,512 --> 00:17:12,060
I was trapped for six days without any food or water.

167
00:17:12,879 --> 00:17:16,040
So the enemy intended to starve you to death, Father.

168
00:17:17,404 --> 00:17:19,741
There is something even more important than that...

169
00:17:19,765 --> 00:17:20,593
What is it?

170
00:17:20,739 --> 00:17:23,455
If only I could retrieve the decree I wrote that night...

171
00:17:23,999 --> 00:17:25,760
Wasn't it burned?

172
00:17:25,909 --> 00:17:27,994
However, I wrote that on tanned leather,

173
00:17:28,018 --> 00:17:32,639
so it might have survived the fire. Sapphire, could you go fetch it?

174
00:17:32,880 --> 00:17:33,206
Yes.

175
00:17:51,179 --> 00:17:53,000
He really got us good!

176
00:17:58,138 --> 00:17:59,400
It's the Ribbon Knight!

177
00:18:04,906 --> 00:18:05,793
What?

178
00:18:06,569 --> 00:18:07,866
The Ribbon Knight?

179
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:08,920
Are you talking in your sleep?

180
00:18:09,529 --> 00:18:12,500
Security is far too strict for anyone to get in.

181
00:18:12,819 --> 00:18:13,980
You idiot!

182
00:18:38,560 --> 00:18:39,713
Found it!

183
00:18:39,999 --> 00:18:41,120
Something is shining right here!

184
00:18:42,509 --> 00:18:44,060
It's too dark to see.

185
00:18:44,520 --> 00:18:45,500
You're in the way!

186
00:18:45,540 --> 00:18:46,399
Pardon me!

187
00:18:46,849 --> 00:18:48,100
Lend me some light!

188
00:18:49,889 --> 00:18:50,663
Can you tell what it says?

189
00:18:52,459 --> 00:18:53,740
Don't worry, I can read it clearly.

190
00:18:53,985 --> 00:18:54,784
Thank you very much!

191
00:18:55,889 --> 00:18:57,366
Don't mention it.

192
00:19:17,699 --> 00:19:19,673
Grand Duke Duralumin!

193
00:19:21,373 --> 00:19:22,480
Please read this.

194
00:19:30,180 --> 00:19:33,480
Anyway, these flyers are pasted all over town.

195
00:19:34,709 --> 00:19:38,366
"Gather in front of the castle gates at 10 a.m. today, Ribbon Knight..."

196
00:19:38,391 --> 00:19:40,246
What if something bad happens!

197
00:19:40,271 --> 00:19:41,116
Don't be stupid!

198
00:19:41,140 --> 00:19:42,820
You'll see something interesting!

199
00:19:46,223 --> 00:19:46,900
What should we do?

200
00:19:47,026 --> 00:19:48,200
Drive them off!

201
00:19:48,240 --> 00:19:50,313
Shoot yourself at them or fire the cannons, just drive them off!

202
00:19:50,559 --> 00:19:52,573
But there are way too many of them! We can't do a thing!

203
00:19:53,340 --> 00:19:55,000
What are you trying to do?!

204
00:20:26,839 --> 00:20:28,639
Everyone, there is someone I want you to see!

205
00:20:29,154 --> 00:20:29,888
Duralumin!

206
00:20:30,220 --> 00:20:30,660
Nylon!

207
00:20:31,040 --> 00:20:32,040
Take a good look!

208
00:20:39,239 --> 00:20:43,127
The Queen?! How did she escape from the Coffin Tower... wait, what?!

209
00:20:48,873 --> 00:20:50,419
N-No way... But...

210
00:20:57,886 --> 00:21:00,186
The King is alive!

211
00:21:09,439 --> 00:21:13,380
I was trapped in the castle dungeon by someone and nearly killed.

212
00:21:13,634 --> 00:21:15,780
Regrettably, I don't know who was behind it.

213
00:21:16,139 --> 00:21:17,900
But I survived and was rescued.

214
00:21:18,144 --> 00:21:19,520
Thanks to the Ribbon Knight.

215
00:21:31,226 --> 00:21:33,345
Come, Father. Let's go inside the castle.

216
00:21:34,645 --> 00:21:35,645
You cannot enter.

217
00:21:35,814 --> 00:21:37,120
You are no longer the King.

218
00:21:37,144 --> 00:21:38,900
Plastic is the King now.

219
00:21:39,380 --> 00:21:40,380
Silence, Duralumin!

220
00:21:40,639 --> 00:21:42,900
This castle belongs to me and my heir, Sapphire!

221
00:21:43,254 --> 00:21:44,479
Heir, you say?

222
00:21:44,569 --> 00:21:49,306
Everyone knows that by Silverland law, a woman cannot be an heir.

223
00:21:49,434 --> 00:21:52,279
Exactly. Until I change that foolish law. And I have changed it.

224
00:21:52,304 --> 00:21:54,280
You can't just change it on a whim.

225
00:21:54,384 --> 00:21:55,460
Not without proof!

226
00:21:55,589 --> 00:21:56,680
The proof is right here.

227
00:21:56,959 --> 00:21:59,140
Official proof stamped with the royal seal.

228
00:21:59,559 --> 00:22:02,153
I wrote this and affixed my seal before I was locked away.

229
00:22:02,294 --> 00:22:03,601
Damn it!

230
00:22:03,820 --> 00:22:07,260
Now, I shall announce the decree changing the law before all our people.

231
00:22:09,959 --> 00:22:13,480
<i>I hereby change the law of Silverland that forbids women from taking the throne!</i>

232
00:22:13,824 --> 00:22:18,700
<i>In the name of the King, I hereby decree that a woman may become queen and rule this land.</i>

233
00:22:21,239 --> 00:22:22,239
Mother!

234
00:22:24,359 --> 00:22:27,373
Hey, Papa, so I don't have to be king anymore?

235
00:22:28,239 --> 00:22:29,886
Fool, shut your mouth!

236
00:22:30,259 --> 00:22:32,619
Really? I'm really not king anymore?

237
00:22:32,744 --> 00:22:34,320
That's right, confound it!

238
00:22:36,124 --> 00:22:38,153
Ooh, that is so cool!

239
00:22:42,689 --> 00:22:43,689
Come, let's step inside.

240
00:22:50,100 --> 00:22:53,379
Curse them! Do they think I will just back down like this?

241
00:22:55,360 --> 00:22:56,360
Princess Sapphire!

242
00:22:57,179 --> 00:23:01,100
Princess, it isn't right for a princess to be dressed like a boy.

243
00:23:04,009 --> 00:23:05,420
Thank you, young lady.

244
00:23:07,960 --> 00:23:08,960
Thank you so much.

245
00:23:09,614 --> 00:23:12,700
But I still want to dress as a boy for now.

246
00:23:13,264 --> 00:23:17,879
I'll stay like this until the evil is gone and true peace comes to this kingdom.

247
00:23:18,369 --> 00:23:20,940
I'll keep this dress safe until then.

248
00:24:06,620 --> 00:24:10,240
♪ Tarari Ratta Ritta Ratta Rattattaa ♪
-

249
00:24:10,241 --> 00:24:13,601
♪ Kyahoo! Kyahoo! Kyahoo! ♪
Yahoo! Yahoo! Yahoo!

250
00:24:13,602 --> 00:24:17,372
♪ Tarari Ratta Ritta Ratta Rattattaa ♪
-

251
00:24:17,373 --> 00:24:20,534
♪ Kyahoo! Kyahoo! Kyahoo! ♪
Yahoo! Yahoo! Yahoo!

252
00:24:20,535 --> 00:24:24,348
♪ Sen'nen man'nen hyakuman-nen ♪
A thousand years, ten thousand years, a million years,

253
00:24:24,349 --> 00:24:27,645
♪ Ribbon de tsunagou ichioku-nen ♪
Let’s connect with ribbons for a billion years!

254
00:24:27,646 --> 00:24:31,651
♪ Akuma ga kute mo arashi ga kute mo ♪
Even if demons come, even if storms arrive,

255
00:24:31,652 --> 00:24:35,090
♪ tsunaida kokoro wa hanarenai ♪
Our bonded hearts will never part.

256
00:24:35,091 --> 00:24:38,711
♪ Tarari Ratta Ritta Ratta Rattattaa ♪
-

257
00:24:38,712 --> 00:24:42,072
♪ Kyahoo! Kyahoo! Kyahoo! ♪
